2026-11-04T04:18:52.5775728Z         """Regression test for a real incident caught live during this validation pass:
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5775925Z         running `kriya analyze` against a scratch project whose config didn't override
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5776197Z         paths.skills silently wrote a new auto-generated skill into the REAL Kriya
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5776401Z         repo's own shared skills/ directory - the exact same class of incident already
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5776539Z         documented multiple times in this project's history.
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5776622Z     
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5776830Z         Uses a FAKE global-skills-dir (patched via get_global_skills_dir, which is what
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5777010Z         the guard itself calls) rather than the real one, so this test - which is
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5777206Z         deliberately exercising the "resolves to the shared dir" scenario - never
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5777398Z         itself risks writing into the real repo's actual skills/ directory, matching
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5777568Z         the exact hygiene lesson this whole guard exists because of."""
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5777678Z         project_dir = tmp_path / "project"
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5777787Z         project_dir.mkdir()
2026-11-04T04:18:52.5777953Z         (project_dir / "app.py").write_text("def foo():\n    pass\n")
